      "description": "Watch Torino vs AC Milan highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 23, 2026. The Stadio Olimpico Grande Torino set the stage for a compelling Serie A encounter as Torino welcomed AC Milan for a high-stakes clash. With both teams looking to establish early-season momentum, the match promised a tactical battle between two of Italy's historic sides. A Tactical Stalemate in the Opening Half On August 23, 2026 , the match kicked off with both sides showing significant defensive discipline. Torino looked to catch the visitors off guard early, with Giovanni Simeone frequently testing the offside trap, while AC Milan struggled to find their rhythm in the final third. Pervis Estupiñán saw a header blocked during a rare foray forward, but clear-cut chances remained at a premium. Despite defensive blunders from Saul Coco and Gvidas Gineitis that briefly threatened the hosts' stability, the first half concluded without a breakthrough, leaving everything to play for in the second period. Milan’s Quickfire Double Shakes Turin The game sparked into life after the interval, particularly following the introduction of Luka Modrić in the 57th minute. Shortly after a VAR check denied AC Milan a potential penalty, the visitors seized control. In the 64th minute, Adrien Rabiot turned provider, setting up Alphadjo Cissé for a clinical right-footed finish. The lead was doubled just three minutes later; a key pass from Modrić found Samuel Chukwueze , who crossed for Rabiot to fire home a superb left-footed volley. Suddenly, the visitors held a commanding 2-0 lead and seemed to be cruising toward victory. Late Drama as Torino Fight Back Refusing to capitulate, Torino threw everything forward in the closing stages. Alieu Njie came agonisingly close to scoring in the 75th minute, but his effort rattled the post. As the clock ticked into stoppage time, the home fans were given a glimmer of hope. In the 93rd minute, Che Adams produced a stunning volley from a Gvidas Gineitis cross to make it 1-2. Despite the frantic final moments and a desperate push for an equalizer, AC Milan maintained their composure to secure a hard-fought away win."
